      "map": "map.html#tree-8",
      "mapX": 47.9,
      "mapY": 32,
      "description": "Also a common sight in Cambodia, especially in suburban or rural areas, this tree is renowned mostly for its agricultural and environmental uses. Its ability to tolerate poor soil and fix nitrogen makes it a valuable component in restoring environmental balance to degraded sites, and its light, durable wood makes it a favorite among artisans and woodworkers. Fun fact: It has an incredibly high density that makes it almost immune to dents.",
      "cite": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buxus_sempervirens",
      "id": "8"
