      "mapX": 47,
      "mapY": 60.3,
      "description": "A sight deeply interwoven into Southeast Asian culture and traditions, frangipani flowers have long been revered as symbols of purity, immortality, and divinity. Many have used it as a popular offering to gods and deities, and in Cambodia, Apsara dancers have long adorned their hair with these flowers in traditional dances. Fun fact: The name Champei, which is a popular girls’ name in Cambodia, actually translates to Frangipani flower.",
      "cite": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plumeria_obtusa",
